tool_extras.jsonl.gz\n\nSafe\n\n40.6 MB xet\n  * toolsets.jsonl.gz\n\nSafe\n\n1.05 GB xet--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/alexar76/warden/tree)\nciteturn7search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago;     Reads the MCP configs of Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor, VS Code and Windsurf, connects to every server they start, and vets the tool definitions before a model sees them. ... In a repository, `warden.lock.json` turns a change in tool definitions into a reviewable diff, and CI fails on a new or changed server.\nThe error includes rule codes and a `pins status` hint.\n    \n    | Options | Default / behavior |\n    |---|---|\n    | `--policy file.json` | Strict JSON policy file; invalid files stop startup |\n    | `--feed URL --feed-key HEX` | Signed MOMUS feed; refused without the key; 10 s timeout, 24 h freshness, persisted anti-rollback |\n    | `--state-dir DIR` | Persistent pins and feed state: `WARDEN_STATE_DIR`, `XDG_STATE_HOME/warden`, `~/.local/state/warden` |\n    | `--verdict-log FILE` | Full verdict JSONL including ruleset version/digest; off by default |\n    | `--audit-only` | Diagnostic mode; off by default |\n    \n    ## Scan every server your clients start\n    \n    ```bash\n    npx -y @aimarket/warden@0.16.0 scan\n    ```\n    \n    Reads the MCP configs of Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor, VS Code and Windsurf, connects to every server they start, and vets the tool definitions before a model sees them. It prints a table, JSON, SARIF or Markdown, and exits 1 when a server is blocked; `--no-launch` starts nothing. In a repository, `warden.lock.json` turns a change in tool definitions into a reviewable diff, and CI fails on a new or changed server. Also as a GitHub Action (`uses: alexar76/warden@v0.16.0`), pre-commit hooks and a Claude Code plugin (`/plugin marketplace add alexar76/warden`). `--histor` asks the public HISTOR log whether a server serves you what it serves everyone; for a remote server it sends the endpoint and a digest, for a stdio server started from npm or PyPI the package name (`npm:<name>`, `pypi:<name>`, which HISTOR runs in a gVisor sandbox) and a digest — never tool text. An opt-in classifier (`--classifier-url`, `--classifier-model`) adds the reading of a model you choose, local or hosted, for what no rule names. See the [scan guide](docs/scan.md). How it compares with two other scanners, on the same servers: [scanner comparison](docs/scanner-comparison.md).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAttested Memory API — Docs, OpenAPI & Kin Score | APIs.io (https://apis.io/providers/attestedmemory-net/)\nciteturn7search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; #### Attestedmemory Net Authentication ...       url: data-model/attestedmemory-net-data-model.yml\n      integrated with the open AIMarket ecosystem.\n    url: https://artifacts.apis.io/attestedmemory-net/apis.yml\n    x-type: company\n    x-source: harvest:mcp-registry\n    x-tier: profiled\n    x-tier-reason: enrichment pass 2026-11-02 (modular-v1; was harvest)\n    specificationVersion: '0.20'\n    created: '2026-11-02'\n    modified: '2026-11-02'\n    tags:\n    - Company\n    - Software-as-a-Service\n    - Verifiable Memory\n    - AI Agents\n    - USDC\n    tags_raw:\n    - Company\n    - SaaS\n    - Verifiable Memory\n    - AI Agents\n    - USDC\n    maintainers:\n    - FN: Kin Lane\n      email: kin@apievangelist.com\n    - FN: APIs.json\n      email: info@apis.io\n    common:\n    - type: AgenticAccess\n      url: agentic-access/attestedmemory-net-agentic-access.yml\n    - type: Plans\n      url: plans/attestedmemory-net-plans-pricing.yml\n    - type: Spectral\n      url: rules/attestedmemory-net-rules.yml\n    - type: JSONLD\n      url: json-ld/attestedmemory-net-context.jsonld\n    - type: Vocabulary\n      url: vocabulary/attestedmemory-net-vocabulary.yml\n    - type: DataModel\n      url: 